{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011SVA66UEjhdoQpCEeWR4Dm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the workspace's `CLAUDE.md`, here's what this project is:\n\n- **It's John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\" (Ghost World Labs / GWL-M)** â€” a research workspace at `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\` for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. Explicitly a research project, not a production system; most of its ~80 root files are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs), with a smaller set of runnable code.\n\n- **The shipping deliverable is a Next.js master GUI** (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) â€” launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`, a custom Next.js + WebSocket server (`server.mjs`) on port 3001 that spawns and supervises agent terminals (Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and Alpha-class agents).\n\n- **It runs agents on the OpenClaw runtime** (MIT-licensed, global npm package). The GUI dispatches turns through `agent-chat.mjs` â†’ `openclaw agent`, with per-agent provider/model routing driven by the canonical `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`.\n\n- **The active agent vehicle is `alpha-v0`** â€” a daily-use general-purpose \"t2r\" (tasteâ†’reason) agent routed through a dispatcher (`brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`), with a $100/month wallet cap, a 7-skill bundle, and per-project transcripts. A set of research/legacy agents (alpha, sigma, prime-coder, etc.) sit behind a toggle.\n\n- **It ships a \"sovereign t2r harness\"** â€” a custom brain-agnostic ReAct harness (`gwl-t2r-brain/harness/`, `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs`) built for cost-efficient, cache-aware, provider-portable agent loops. M1 is feature-complete for Google + Anthropic; recent work (on branch `foreman/run`) added 6 default-OFF flag-gated orchestration waves (clarify/progress/approval-gate/verify/replan/command-sandbox).\n\n- **The architectural thesis is \"distill from frontier into small local students\"** â€” three intended brains (Opus-4.8 baseline Â· t2r efficient Â· fully-local/sovereign ~7â€“8B OSS on the box's RTX 4070), plus a skill ecosystem (expert-coder, deep-research, project-manager, etc.) linked into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and OpenClaw from a master skill repo.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and memory index (self-description), not from independently reading the code. If you want, I can verify any specific claim (e.g., that the GUI actually runs, or that the harness tests pass) against the filesystem."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7051,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7051,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2771d3e-4038-4df1-a930-cd913691c005","uuid":"9a413f6a-f08e-49e4-aff8-22a393ed2946","request_id":"req_011Cc38r379a7FRETEE4w88H"}
